    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.5,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"short_to_ground\",\n      \"components\": [\"U6\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U6.13\", \"U6.14\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The SKW92A module's LAN_PORT3_TX+ (pin 13) and LAN_PORT3_TX- (pin 14) are both members of the GND net, so the differential transmit outputs of switch port 3 are hard-tied to ground.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Unused Ethernet PHY transmit pins should be left unconnected (or handled per the datasheet), not shorted to ground. The spec does not describe any intentional tie of these pins, and the other LAN pins are not similarly grounded.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U6\\\") (pin \\\"13\\\") (pinfunction \\\"LAN_PORT3_TX+\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U6\\\") (pin \\\"14\\\") (pinfunction \\\"LAN_PORT3_TX-\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\"))\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"Driving or pulling these pins against ground can load or damage the PHY output drivers on that port and may disturb the switch's Ethernet/PHY behaviour.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.45\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"footprint_mismatch\",\n      \"components\": [\"C4\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"C4.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(C4-Pad1)\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"C4 is a 0.1 \u00b5F capacitor whose footprint is an inductor land pattern (L_0805). Its pin 1 sits on a single-node net with nothing else connected, so the part does not decouple anything.\",\n      \"expected\": \"A 0.1 \u00b5F capacitor should use a capacitor footprint and be connected across a supply rail and GND as a decoupling or bypass element.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(footprint \\\"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"59\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(C4-Pad1)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C4 unconnected-_C4-Pad1_ 0 0.1u\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The decoupling capacitor is ineffective, and the wrong footprint could cause a mis-placed or mis-soldered part during assembly.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_value\",\n      \"components\": [\"C2\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"C2.1\", \"C2.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"Net-(U11-K)\", \"Net-(Q3-D)\"],\n      \"observed\": \"C2 is a 4.7 \u00b5F/25 V capacitor in the charge-pump flying-capacitor position between the switching node and the rectifier node, where the other flying-capacitor equivalent is 1 \u00b5F.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The spec states the EPD driver values match the Pervasive Displays reference, with C2 at 1 \u00b5F/25 V (default) or 1 \u00b5F/6.3 V (G1). A 4.7 \u00b5F value is a deviation from that reference.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(comp (ref \\\"C2\\\") (value \\\"4.7uF/25V\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"C2 default: 1 \u00b5F/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 \u00b5F/25 V\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"A larger flying capacitor changes the charge-pump transfer and ripple behaviour of the display's boosted supply, which may affect panel drive voltages.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist shows the SKW92A's LAN_PORT3 transmit pins tied directly to GND, which is the most likely deviation from the intended design. A decoupling capacitor with an inductor footprint and a floating pin, and a flying capacitor value that departs from the referenced 1 \u00b5F, are lower-confidence additional concerns.\"\n}",
